# Smart Sea Belt – Backwater Test Report

## 1. Test Overview

The Smart Sea Belt prototype was tested in a controlled backwater environment to evaluate its basic functional operation and system integration.

The testing was carried out to verify the communication, monitoring, emergency-alert and safety functions of the prototype.

## 2. Test Environment

- Test Environment: Backwater
- Test Type: Prototype Functional Testing
- Test Purpose: Functional and system-level validation
- Testing Status: Prototype tested successfully at functional level

## 3. System Functions Tested

The following prototype functions were tested:

- Smart Watch operation
- Heart-rate monitoring
- Motion and fall detection
- SOS emergency activation
- GPS/location functionality
- Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) communication
- Boat Hub operation
- LoRa communication
- Base Unit communication
- Emergency alert mechanism
- Flotation mechanism
- Rudder diversion mechanism

## 4. System Communication Flow

The prototype follows the communication flow:

Smart Watch
↓
BLE
↓
Boat Hub
↓
LoRa
↓
Base Unit

The test was used to verify the functional interaction between the major system modules.

## 5. Test Observations

The prototype was operated in the backwater environment and the major safety and communication functions were checked.

The testing provided practical validation of the prototype's integrated operation under the tested conditions.

## 6. Test Result

The backwater test demonstrated prototype-level functional operation of the Smart Sea Belt system.

The test supports the feasibility of the integrated prototype concept and provides practical evidence for further development and validation.

The results should be considered prototype-level testing and not certification or confirmation of open-sea operational readiness.

## 7. Further Validation

Further testing is required under different operating conditions before the system can be considered for full-scale marine deployment.

Future validation can include:

- Extended-duration testing
- Open-water testing
- Communication-range testing
- Sensor accuracy validation
- Battery endurance testing
- Environmental and weather-condition testing
- Safety and reliability validation

## 8. Evidence

Supporting photographs and test documentation are maintained in the repository under:

`results/`

## 9. Conclusion

The backwater testing provided practical functional validation of the Smart Sea Belt prototype and demonstrated the operation of its major safety, monitoring and communication functions.

The test results will be used to support further prototype improvement and validation.
